Research shows the product is available from some US national manufacturers 
above the minimum recycled content shown.  Some manufacturers do not offer recycled 
content.</NPR><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<NPR>Some manufacturers provide proprietary interlocking connections between some 
thicker available planks, for instance in 8 mm 3/8 inch versions.  These interlocking 
means are typically concealed from view once installed and may provide some 
water-blocking function to help prevent cleaning methods or spills from easily 
passing through flooring installation to substrates below.</NPR><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<NPR>Term "waterproof" is used in some manufacturer's sales literature. When specifying 
flooring, clarify if material is water-resistive and/or interlocking seams are 
water-blocking.  Refrain from using term "waterproof" for any flooring that 
is not a seamless and watertight membrane to prevent misunderstandings of flooring 
performance.</NPR><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<NPR>Tile formats may be referred to as "plank" by manufacturers when units are longer 
than they are wide such that they visually suggest planks.  These can still 
be categorized as tile.</NPR><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/></NTE>
